        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 71-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received patient education regarding inhaler technique and self-management. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Pulse oximetry monitoring was maintained throughout his stay. He is discharged in stable condition and I recommend follow-up spirometry and continued optimisation of his inhaler regimen. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you have any questions.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
